CHAPTER.VERS:
Forasmuch as this people refuseth the waters of 

          Which was a fountain at the foot of mount Zion, out of which ran a small river through the city: meaning, that they of Judah distrusting their own power which was small desired such power and riches as they saw in Syria and Israel.
         Shiloah that flow gently, and rejoice in Rezin and Remaliah's son;
